<%# Two states, both above the table where the rows they explain are.

    REFUSED: the search was not understood, so it selects nothing. Unexplained,
    that is indistinguishable from "no jobs have this problem" — the reading that
    gets someone to close the tab satisfied.

    DEGRADED: a facet was dropped and the rest applied. Browsing proceeds, because
    a typo should not stop you looking. Bulk actions do not, because the filter
    that survived selects a superset of what was typed — see bulk_filter_present?.

    Reuses .rh-warn rather than inventing a state: the bulk cap notice already
    means "read this before you trust the count below". %>
<% if @filter&.invalid? %>
  <div class="rh-warn" role="alert">
    <%= @filter.message %>
    <%= link_to "Clear the search", filter_url(q: nil), class: "rh-sub" %>
  </div>
<% elsif @filter&.degraded? %>
  <div class="rh-warn" role="status">
    <%= @filter.notes.join(" ") %>
    Showing what the rest of the search selects; bulk actions are off until it parses.
  </div>
<% end %>
